        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tom Verlaine, Marti Pellow, Richard Hell, Billy Ficca\n- Bands: Television, Neon Boys, Wet Wet Wet\n- Places: New York City\n\nFacts:\n- Tom Verlaine was born Thomas Miller on December 13, 1949.\n- Tom Verlaine is an American singer, songwriter, and guitarist.\n- Tom Verlaine is best known as the frontman of the New York City rock band Television.\n- The Neon Boys was an early 1970s New York City punk band.\n- The Neon Boys was composed of Tom Verlaine, Richard Hell, and Billy Ficca.\n- Marti Pellow was born Mark McLachlan on March 23, 1965.\n- Marti Pellow is a Scottish singer.\n- Marti Pellow was a lead vocalist and founding member of Wet Wet Wet.\n- Marti Pellow quit Wet Wet Wet in 2017.",
